# Phase 18 `MqClientAdmin` public wrapper closure — 2026-10-21T13:47:48Z

Branch: `phase/18-phase-18-compatibility-closure`
Pinned Java source: `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`

- Found a Rust public-surface gap: Java `MqClientAdmin` declares 19 methods,
  while `MQClientApi::mq_client_admin()` exposed only 8. Added the missing 11
  typed wrappers by routing to the already audited direct Core operations.
- `update_or_create_topic` uses the direct request path. The lower-level
  `MQClientApi::create_topic` also performs local topic-permission validation,
  which Java's `MqClientAdminImpl.updateOrCreateTopic` does not. Added an
  invoked Java case and a Rust scripted regression proving an invalid permission
  is sent to the peer.
- Added the pinned Java interface method-signature inventory to
  `fixtures/admin/query-consume-time-span.json`. The Core integration test
  checks all 19 Java names and compile-calls all 19 Rust wrapper methods.
- Fixture SHA-256:
  `670a5ee121a41def537a4a97c806e5c6d25176917f945742495b5c2995217d62`.

